From fccffe153982bcbaab5aa531aa41826a0b4b4b69 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 02:36:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] ASoC: apple: s8000-mca: add capture over SmartIO (MCA0
 RX)

Add a capture stream when the node has a SmartIO "rx" DMA channel
(MCA0 RX is endpoint 0x29). The generic dmaengine PCM fails the whole
card for a DAI stream without a channel, so without "rx" the DAI keeps
only playback, as before.

RX uses iOS's _setIISConfig_v4 values: RX_CFG 0x132 (0x133 to run),
RX_FIFO_CFG 0x00030004 and slot mask 3. iOS requests the SmartIO depth
with the same per-millisecond formula for both directions; the DMA
driver's validFIFODepth then gives RX min(request, trigger), 192 bytes
at 48 kHz. Each direction gets its own shim record.

TX and RX share the frame, the IRQ mask and the run bit, so they are
now handled per direction. The first prepared direction programs the
whole block as before; the second one only resets and programs its own
half (RESET bit 0 for TX, bit 1 for RX). The frame stops when the last
direction stops, and the route and frame are torn down when the last
one is freed. A direction's FIFO error causes are unmasked only while
it is prepared: playback alone now leaves the RX causes masked (iOS
unmasks them too). Trigger and the IRQ handler serialize the shared
state with a spinlock. debugfs reports the first-error timing per
direction ("last playback stream", "last capture stream").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <maintainer@example.invalid>
